    {
      "id": "duender",
      "name": "Duender",
      "manufacturer": "Irbis3D",
      "aliases": [],
      "notes": "Ender-3 to CoreXY conversion (Irbis3D/Duender). The project ships no Klipper config, so a bare Duender has nothing in printer.objects.list that distinguishes it from any other CoreXY. Deliberately carries no object/kinematics heuristics: a 'corexy' match here would compete with the Voron and RatRig entries on every one of their machines. Hostname only, plus the wizard's manual pick."
    },
    {
      "id": "duender_medusahc",
      "name": "Duender (MedusaHC)",
      "manufacturer": "Irbis3D",
      "aliases": [],
      "notes": "Duender CoreXY (Irbis3D) fitted with the MedusaHC hotend changer. MedusaHC is klipper-toolchanger plus its own pin_watch extra, so the AMS resolves to Tool Changer and AmsBackendToolChanger drives it. Scored on pin_watch and hostname ONLY: toolchanger/tool_count/corexy describe any multi-tool CoreXY and would claim machines that are not this one. The bare-Duender hostname deliberately does NOT appear here, or the 'duender' entry could never outscore this one."
    },
